    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_1a63b6b1b4da8cabaa154b20d2c5e8227938747ea8c2cf4887ffe6960040b39f",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The induction partitions solutions by residue geometry at a prime chosen so p^r matches the original variable scale. In the regular branch, distinct residues make selected tuples rigid through power sums and symmetric-polynomial data, while the remaining common residue class is translated and divided to expose a smaller-scale mean value; in the singular branch, the deficit of distinct residues first reduces the number of patterns, and the same translation-and-division symmetry again yields a smaller-scale mean value.",
