    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_5fc9307bc54f36fdbe0d68cce8989df942ff682abd7a57c9c014b2a49b1c1f9e",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Re-expressing the zeta-sum theorem by the scale N relative to t reveals more than the final error's appearance: fixed-power lengths yield a power saving, a subpower interval yields only nontrivial cancellation, and the unclaimed shorter range marks the present reach of the method. The source then identifies widening that cancellation range as a route to wider near-one zero-free regions while explicitly separating it from any route to the critical line.",
