      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The shift–Taylor step converts the logarithmic oscillation into a bounded-degree polynomial in a product of two independent variables. Repeated Hölder duplication then replaces sparse moment-curve data by a central Vinogradov mean value while leaving coordinatewise coefficient arithmetic in reciprocal-spacing sums; the final parameter balance combines both sources of saving to recover cancellation in the original zeta block.",
